        {
          "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Udbax6z1nbb8HqLCDXi4gM",
          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022:\u0022concepts/bloom-filter.md\u0022,\u0022content\u0022:\u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: Bloom Filter\\ndescription: A probabilistic data structure that efficiently tests set membership with a tunable false-positive rate.\\ntimestamp: 2026-01-06T00:00:00Z\\ntags:\\n  - concept/data-structures\\n  - concept/probabilistic-algorithms\\nconfidence: medium\\nconfidence_reason: \\u0022Single source describing the fundamental mechanism; no corroboration yet.\\u0022\\n---\\n\\nA bloom filter is a probabilistic set-membership structure that answers set membership queries with certainty only for negative cases and probabilistic certainty for positive cases.\\n\\n## Core Mechanism\\n\\nA bloom filter uses:\\n- A **bit array** of fixed size\\n- **k independent hash functions** that map set elements to bit positions\\n\\nWhen inserting an element, the filter hashes the element using all k hash functions and sets the corresponding bits to 1. To test membership, it hashes the query element and checks whether all k corresponding bits are set.\\n\\n## Guarantees and Tradeoffs\\n\\nThe filter provides these semantics:\\n\\n- **Definite negatives**: If any of the k bit positions is 0, the element is definitely not in the set.\\n- **Possible positives**: If all k bit positions are 1, the element may or may not be in the set \\u2014 the result carries a tunable false-positive rate, which decreases as the bit array grows and increases as more elements are added.\\n\\n## Limitations\\n\\n**No enumeration**: A bloom filter cannot list its members; it only tests membership.\\n\\n**No deletion in basic form**: Removing a set bit could break the membership test for other elements that happen to hash to the same position. Variants like counting bloom filters address this constraint by replacing single bits with counters, at the cost of additional space.\\n\\n## Citations\\n\\n[^1]: Source: eval://log-newest-first-placement/sample-09\\n\u0022}"
        }
      ],
